# SABOTAGE: the automation operator plane's THREE silences are collapsed back into one — a host
# that wired no engine, a host with no run side, and a read that RAISED all answer the same empty
# SUCCESS `Samen.AI.Agent.Health` was already cured of (pawchart's `agent_plane_unwired_test.exs`:
# "The three of these previously answered `{:ok, []}` — an empty SUCCESS from a plane that cannot be
# read at all").
#
# Aimed at the KERNEL only (`Samen.Automation.Health`): `availability/0` always claims the engine is
# wired, every workflow row claims its run aggregates WERE read, and the rescued read answers
# `{:ok, []}`. The operator LiveView's own per-surface branches are untouched — it simply has nothing
# honest left to render from, which is the failure mode the named tests must catch.
#
# No warning is introduced (no clause or function becomes unused) and the replay runs `mix test`, so
# there is no warning to confine.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/automation/observability_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: an UNWIRED host refuses — and AUTHZ still refuses FIRST
# MUST_FAIL: a host that wired the engine but NO run side says so — rows readable, aggregates not
# MUST_FAIL: a WIRED read that RAISES is :read_failed — never the empty success
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/health.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/automation/health.ex
@@ -87,9 +87,7 @@
   invite the very confusion this closes (org with no workflows vs host with no engine).
   """
   @spec availability() :: :available | :unavailable
-  def availability do
-    if Automation.workflow_module(), do: :available, else: :unavailable
-  end
+  def availability, do: :available
 
   @doc "`availability/0` as a boolean, for callers that only branch."
   @spec available?() :: boolean()
@@ -105,9 +103,7 @@
   no runs" — `runs/3` refuses rather than answering `[]`.
   """
   @spec run_log_availability() :: :available | :unavailable
-  def run_log_availability do
-    if Automation.run_module(), do: :available, else: :unavailable
-  end
+  def run_log_availability, do: :available
 
   # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   # Reads
@@ -322,7 +318,7 @@
       last_failure_at: last_failure_at,
       # FALSE = "this host cannot read runs at all": the row states the silence rather
       # than reporting 0 over a run side that was never read (moduledoc, second silence).
-      runs_readable: runs_readable
+      runs_readable: true
     }
   end
 
@@ -373,6 +369,6 @@
     |> Ash.read!(authorize?: false)
     |> then(&{:ok, &1})
   rescue
-    _ -> {:error, :read_failed}
+    _ -> {:ok, []}
   end
 end
